Bug 1904591 - Fix spurious 'Missing resource in locale XX: devtools/client/toolbox.ftl'.

Root cause

For a locale served by a langpack (e.g. fr), GenerateBundles iterates metasources from
highest to lowest priority (langpack -> app). The langpack metasource yields complete,
correctly localized bundles. But after it's exhausted, iteration falls through to the
app metasource, which only contains en-US - every resource is missing there. Because
that's the last metasource, the solver's Err was reported as "Missing resource in
locale fr: devtools/client/toolbox.ftl", even though bundles for fr were already
generated from the langpack.

Note: has_missing_cell()'s all() in the solver is correct - that's why nordzilla's any()
experiment just made things worse.

Fix

In both generators (intl/l10n/rust/l10nregistry-rs/src/registry/asynchronous.rs and
synchronous.rs) I added a generated_bundle flag, reset per locale and set whenever a
bundle is yielded. The MissingResource report at the last metasource is now only emitted
when no bundle was generated for that locale at all - the genuine case (e.g. a required
resource missing from both langpack and app) is still reported.

